# Puerto Ink Academy — Cursor Rules

## Tech Stack
- Next.js 15 (App Router, Server Actions, TypeScript)
- Styling: Tailwind CSS, Shadcn UI (Dark theme only, sleek gaming aesthetic)
- Database: PostgreSQL via Drizzle ORM
- Storage: DigitalOcean Spaces (S3 compatible) + CDN
- Auth: Session-based role auth (ADMIN, TEACHER, APPRENTICE)

## Domain Business Rules
- Levels are linear and locked: apprentices can only view their active level.
- Submissions require 8/10 or higher to pass and unlock the next sequence.
- Endless attempts: failed submissions (<8/10) trigger retries and persist in history.
- Dynamic XP: award XP based on score (10 = 100 XP, 9 = 90 XP, 8 = 80 XP, <8 = 0 XP).
- Versioning: edits to lessons create new versions in `level_versions` to preserve historical student data.

## Code Style
- Always use TypeScript with strict types; do not use `any`.
- Keep components modular and mobile-first responsive.
